  "review": [
    "The hymn is Psalm 23 expanded: 1:1–8 is Ps 23:1–4 nearly line for line, the chorus is Zech 4:6 with Ps 121:6 and Isa 4:6 (the shelter from rain), 2:1–8 is Prov 18:10 with Mic 7:8, and 3:1–8 is Ps 34:2 with Ps 34:11 and Ps 145:15.",
    "3:4 מִי נְשָׂאַנִי עַל־שִׁכְמוֹ uses the shepherd's carrying of Luke 15:5 (עַל־כְּתֵפָיו) with the Hebrew שֶׁכֶם, because the stanza is counting the shepherd's acts and not describing a feeling.",
    "3:7–8 keep the psalm's lions-and-hunger image (Ps 34:11) in the same order as the print, so the stanza ends on the contrast between the hungry and the fed."
  ]
